{
  "about": "DW-6 (27 Nov 2026): the DW-5 file plus INC2P, the design team's INC 2P rule for OPX-203 (ruling DW-R12, 26 Nov): INC 2P modules = all modules - (3P + Other + Ballast + Tin Shade lines); OPX-203 = INC 2P modules x the site's module wattage / 1000, in kWp, exact to 0.01. \"site_factor\": \"module_wp\" is the site's wattage (one wattage: its own; mixed, or an OPX-001 line: the Head's default, DW-R14). \"clamp_at_zero\": below 0 is written as 0 with a warning instead of refusing the save. \"warning_check\": \"inc_2p_structures\" warns when the INC 2P module count differs from the modules the 2P structure lines hold; each \"role\": \"check\" driver is one 2P item weighted by the modules one structure holds (2P*N holds 2N), never summed. 1P structures are not in the check (ruled). The key is INC2P so it cannot be confused with R12 (OPX-177, earthing). Every other rule is the DW-5 file's, unchanged. DW-5 (27 Nov 2026): the B-2c file of 24 Nov with one change: R12 (module earthing sets) reads the open group \"all modules\" (OPX-001 and one item per wattage, OPX-275..278) instead of OPX-001 alone. \"open\": true means the loader adds the members listed and never removes a member the Head's catalogue form added. B-2c (24 Nov 2026): Praveen's Master BOQ Excel formulas (Master_BOQ.xlsx, Sheet1, column E) as BOQ formula rules, with only his ruled corrections: the 10 kW inverter counts in every per-inverter rule (F4-14); R20 counts DCDBs and every ACDB (F4-15); the 100 mm fittings come from the 100 mm pipe (G2); packs, pieces and metres round up (F4-17); at least 1 only when the drivers are above 0 (G3). THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH: load_formula_rules --apply makes the active rules match it, including switching back on a rule switched off with --deactivate. R24 and R25 are active (Zuber, Q3, 24 Nov): INC work Tin Shade / Ballast follows the Tin Shade and Ballast counts in Nos, which fix_tin_shade_ballast --apply-counts writes.",
